{
  "published": "2026-10-11",
  "title": "WhatsApp Business API Pricing 2026: Service Messages No Longer Free",
  "meta_description": "Since 2026-10-01 each business phone number gets 1,000 free service messages a month and then pays per message.",
  "lead": "Since 2026-10-01 service replies are no longer free. Each business phone number gets 1,000 free service messages a month, then pays the market's rate. Utility templates sent inside the 24-hour window are now charged. An account with no payment method stops delivering replies past 1,000. The next possible price change is 2027-01-01.",
  "read_line": "Prices read on Meta's pricing page (updated 2026-09-30) and its USD and BRL rate cards effective 2026-10-01, on 2026-10-10 and 2026-10-16. Meta's fees only, before any provider's markup and before tax.",
  "free_service_messages_per_number": 1000,
  "changes": {
    "heading": "What changed on 2026-10-01",
    "intro": "Each row gives the rule until 2026-09-30 and from 2026-10-01.",
    "columns": [
      "Message",
      "Until 2026-09-30",
      "From 2026-10-01"
    ],
    "rows": [
      {
        "label": "Service messages (non-template replies inside the 24-hour customer service window)",
        "cells": [
          "Free, with no monthly limit (since 2024-11-01)",
          "1,000 free per business phone number a month; from the 1,001st, the market's service rate. Unused free messages do not roll over"
        ]
      },
      {
        "label": "Service messages from eligible governments and non-profits",
        "cells": [
          "Free, with no monthly limit",
          "Still free past the 1,000 through 2027-12-31, for organisations Meta deems eligible. Eligible: government departments and agencies, inter-governmental organisations, and community non-profits, including public health, crisis response, disaster relief and non-partisan civic engagement"
        ]
      },
      {
        "label": "Non-template messages from AI Providers' general-purpose AI assistants",
        "cells": [
          "Allowed only where Meta is legally required to permit them. Meta has charged $0.0625 per message in Brazil since 2026-03-11",
          "The 2026-10-01 changes do not apply to them, so they get no 1,000 free messages. Brazil: $0.0625 per message. Users in the EU and EEA (Austria, Belgium, Bulgaria, Croatia, Cyprus, the Czech Republic, Denmark, Estonia, Finland, France, Germany, Greece, Hungary, Iceland, Ireland, Italy, Latvia, Liechtenstein, Lithuania, Luxembourg, Malta, the Netherlands, Norway, Poland, Portugal, Romania, Slovakia, Slovenia, Spain and Sweden): no charge since 2026-05-13. Türkiye: permitted since 2026-10-15. Meta does not charge. No end date given."
        ]
      },
      {
        "label": "Utility templates sent in reply inside an open customer service window",
        "cells": [
          "Free (since 2025-07-01)",
          "Charged at the market's utility rate"
        ]
      },
      {
        "label": "Service messages past the 1,000 free ones, on an account with no payment method",
        "cells": [
          "Delivered",
          "Not delivered"
        ]
      },
      {
        "label": "Webhook `pricing.type` of a charged service or in-window utility message",
        "cells": [
          "`free_customer_service`",
          "`regular`"
        ]
      },
      {
        "label": "Rates",
        "cells": [
          "",
          "Meta updated 40 rates. Bangladesh, Iraq, Kazakhstan, Kuwait, Morocco, Nepal, Oman, Sri Lanka and Ukraine moved from a regional rate to their own. Marketing rose in Kuwait, Mexico, Morocco, Saudi Arabia, the United Arab Emirates, Rest of Asia Pacific and Rest of Middle East"
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  "rates": {
    "heading": "Rates per message by market",
    "intro": "Rates are per delivered message in US dollars, by the user's country calling code. Every country on Meta's rate card has a row in the table. Thirty-nine countries have their own rates. Regional countries show their region's rates, with the region named in brackets. Any country with no row pays the Other rate. At list rates, utility, authentication and service cost the same in each market. Past a monthly volume, utility and authentication cost less: in North America, past 80,000 utility or 100,000 authentication messages a month. Every business pays the table's rates, except AI Providers offering a general-purpose AI assistant. Meta permits these only in Brazil, the EU and EEA, and Türkiye. In Brazil they pay $0.0625 per non-template message. In the EU and EEA, including Germany, France, Spain and the Netherlands, Meta does not charge them. In Türkiye, since 2026-10-15, Meta does not charge. No end date is given. A business using AI to answer its own customers pays the table's rates. For users in Brazil, BRL rates are R$0.3217 per marketing message and R$0.035 per utility, authentication or service message, when the account is billed in Brazilian reais.",
